  "roleRuleText": "{roleId, select, voleur{Wake the Thief. He may swap his card with one of the two undealt cards, or keep his own.} cupidon{Wake Cupid. He picks two players who fall in love, then the two lovers open their eyes to recognise each other before going back to sleep.} voyante{Wake the Seer. She points at a player, whose role you reveal to her.} loup_garou{Wake the Werewolves. Together they choose their victim.} sorciere{Wake the Witch. Show her the wolves' victim. She may use her life potion and/or her death potion.} villageois{No night action.} petite_fille{No call: she may peek during the Werewolves' turn, at her own risk.} chasseur{No night action: when he dies (day or night), he immediately eliminates a player of his choice.} renard{Wake the Fox (optional). He points at a player: you tell him whether a Werewolf is among that player and their two living neighbours. If there is none, he loses his power for good.} deux_soeurs{Wake the Two Sisters: they recognise each other, then go back to sleep. Optional after night 1, every other night.} montreur_d_ours{Wake the Bear Tamer on night 1 to know who he is. Every morning, after the victims, you growl if one of his two living neighbours is a Werewolf.} enfant_sauvage{Wake the Wild Child on night 1: they pick a role model. They stay a villager while the model lives; when the model dies they become a Werewolf and wake with the Werewolves.} chien_loup{Just before the Werewolves on night 1, quietly ask the Wolf-Hound to choose: villager or Werewolf, for good. If they choose the Werewolves, they wake with them every night.} loup_garou_blanc{They wake with the Werewolves every night. Every other night, call them alone: they may eliminate a Werewolf. They win alone if they are the last one alive.} infect_pere_des_loups{They wake with the Werewolves. Once per game, after them, they may infect the Werewolves' victim instead of letting them die: the victim secretly becomes a Werewolf and keeps their power.} grand_mechant_loup{They wake with the Werewolves, then alone a second time as long as no Werewolf, Wild Child or Wolf-Hound has died: they devour a second victim, never a Werewolf.} ancien{No call. They survive the wolves' 1st attack (without telling) and die on the 2nd. The village vote, the poison or the Hunter's shot kill them at once: the villagers then lose their powers for the rest of the game.} chevalier{No call. If the wolves devour him, the first wolf to his left catches the disease: it dies as the next night begins (or ends, per the setting), announced as dead of disease.} joueur_de_flute{Wake the Piper every night, after the Witch: they charm 2 players. Then wake the charmed players so they recognise each other. They win as soon as every other living player is charmed.} joueurs_charmes{Wake every player already charmed so they recognise each other, then put them back to sleep.} ange{No call. The game starts with a debate and a vote before night 1. Eliminated at that vote or during night 1, they win alone; alive on day 2, they become a Simple Villager (and give up their goal if they are in love).} salvateur{Wake the Defender before the Werewolves: they point at a player, protected from the Werewolves tonight (themselves included, but never the same player two nights in a row). It does not protect from charm or infection.} idiot_du_village{No call. Voted against by the village, they show their card and are pardoned: nobody is eliminated that day, and they no longer vote for the rest of the game. Devoured by the Werewolves or shot by the Hunter, they die; if they were Sheriff, the honor is lost.} bouc_emissaire{No call. On a tied vote they are eliminated, even if they were not among the tied. Eliminated, they name who may vote on the next day: the others have no vote.} trois_freres{Wake the Three Brothers: they recognise each other, then go back to sleep. Optional after night 1, every other night.} villageois_villageois{No night call. At the deal he shows his card to everyone: note who it is before the village goes to sleep. He has no power.} juge_begue{Wake the Wandering Judge: he silently shows you the secret sign by which he will call for a second vote. Once per game, during a vote.} abominable_sectaire{No night call. Before night 1, divide the village in two groups by something everyone can see (side of the table, clothing...), then note them. The Manipulator wins alone when the whole group he is not in is eliminated: he then leaves the game.} servante_devouee{No night call. Right after a vote, before the eliminated player's card is turned over, she may reveal herself and take their role: the new role plays from the next night on, as on a first night. Once, and not if she is in love.} comedien{Lay three power cards (no Werewolf) face up. Every night, wake the Actor: he chooses one and uses its power that night, when that role is called; the card then leaves the game.} other{}}",
